{
  if (normalizePath("s3n://", mustWork = FALSE) == "s3n://") {
    normalizePath(path, mustWork = FALSE)
  }
  else {
    if (substr(path,1,6)=='s3n://') {
      path
    } else {
      normalizePath(path, mustWork = FALSE)
    }
  }
}
```

With reference to issue #432. The function below does not return anything when the if statement evaluates to false.

```{r}
spark_normalize_path <- function(path) {
  # only normalize paths in OS that behave correctly for custom
  # protocols, in windows, this is not the case. See #432
  if (normalizePath("s3n://", mustWork = FALSE) == "s3n://") {
    normalizePath(path, mustWork = FALSE)
  }
}
```

I propose something of the form:

```{r}
spark_normalize_path <- function(path) {
  # only normalize paths in OS that behave correctly for custom
  # protocols, in windows, this is not the case. See #432
  if (normalizePath("s3n://", mustWork = FALSE) == "s3n://") {
    normalizePath(path, mustWork = FALSE)
  } else {
    # for windows users
    if (substr(path,1,6)=='s3n://') {
      return(path) # to cater for an S3 path
    } else {
      return(normalizePath(path, mustWork = FALSE)) # to still handle relative paths
    }
  }
}
```

